        'faq' => [
            ['q' => 'What does the Chronological Age calculator work out?', 'a' => <<<'TXT'
            It returns years and months and days and chronological age in days from date of birth and date of assessment. The relationship is getYear(Date of assessment) - getYear(Date of birth) - if_else(getMonth(Date of assessment) < getMonth(Date of birth), 1, if_else(getMonth(Date of assessment) == getMonth(Date of birth), if_else(getDate(Date of assessment) < getDate(Date of birth), 1, 0), 0)).
